{"id":"5e921de215cd9b4c1c129473198c94b8c4e4556c","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"5e921de215cd9b4c1c129473198c94b8c4e4556c","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".buildkite/test_areas/models_basic.yaml","lines":["@@ -401,6 +401,10 @@ steps:","   - vllm/config/compilation.py","   - vllm/v1/attention/backends/short_conv_attn.py","   - vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/checkpoint.py","+  - vllm/v1/hisparse/","+  - vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/hisparse/","+  - vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/index_group.py","+  - vllm/model_executor/warmup/qwen4_exp_qsa_warmup.py","   - tests/models/qwen4_exp/","   commands:","     - >-"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/design/hisparse.md","lines":["@@ -30,10 +30,13 @@ configured, `MultiConnector` composes it with `HiSparseConnector`."," "," `host_pool_gib` is configured on `HiSparseConnector` and is the usable"," host-cache capacity per data-parallel replica, not a node-wide memory budget.","-Tensor-parallel ranks hold replicated views of that logical cache. Those views","-may use private per-rank backing or one shared","-physical allocation without changing the configured capacity. Physical host","-memory consumption is therefore topology- and implementation-dependent. The","+MLA tensor-parallel ranks hold replicated views of that logical cache, using","+private per-rank backing or one shared physical allocation. QSA stores full K/V","+heads in private per-rank pools, with each rank writing its own shard. Its","+logical capacity counts each unique K/V head once; heads replicated when TP","+exceeds the K/V head count still consume physical memory in each rank's pool.","+Padding also contributes to physical allocation, not logical capacity. Physical","+host memory consumption is therefore topology- and implementation-dependent. The"," realized capacity may be slightly smaller because the budget is rounded down"," to complete host blocks."," ","@@ -45,6 +48,29 @@ host only their active tail pages, plus one request being admitted at its full"," footprint. Host-pool metrics are listed in"," [Metrics](../usage/metrics.md#hisparse-kv-connector-metrics)."," ","+## QSA models","+","+For Qwen4Exp QSA models, configure `HiSparseConnector` to offload the main K/V","+cache.","+","+```bash","+vllm serve QSA_MODEL \\","+  --kv-transfer-config '{\"kv_connector\":\"HiSparseConnector\",\"kv_role\":\"kv_both\",\"kv_connector_extra_config\":{\"host_pool_gib\":8}}'","+```","+","+The device layout resolves to `BLNHC`, so one copy row holds a token's K and V","+for every local K/V head. HiSparse leaves compressed indexer keys, raw-key rings","+and recurrent state in their normal GPU cache groups. With prefix caching,","+prefixes are reused at whole scheduler-page boundaries; matching tokens past","+the boundary are recomputed.","+","+QSA does not yet implement decode context parallelism, even without HiSparse.","+The current HiSparse configuration also rejects DCP.","+","+QSA P/D with HiSparse requires a separate NIXL integration for mixed host/GPU","+cache registration and transfer-group mapping across P and D. It is not yet","+supported by this implementation.","+"," ## Ownership"," "," | Thing | Owner | What “owner” means |","@@ -68,8 +94,8 @@ sees only device pools."," The source group has `block_pool_id=None`; device-pool consumers must narrow it"," before indexing, so host ownership cannot masquerade as a numeric GPU pool."," ","-For single-node MP tensor parallelism, every TP worker maps the same pinned host","-pool and uses the same block and layer offsets. MLA source KV is replicated","+For MLA with single-node MP tensor parallelism, every TP worker maps the same","+pinned host pool and uses the same block and layer offsets. Source KV is replicated"," across TP ranks, so this stores one physical copy instead of one copy per rank."," TP rank 0 writes the shared host pool; peers wait on its IPC events before"," reading it. Other executor and parallel layouts retain private per-rank pools.","@@ -148,31 +174,25 @@ behind it."," "," ## P/D import target"," ","-The decoder chooses the landing target once per request from the normal cache","-admission calculation. If the complete imported prefix fits the device pools,","-NIXL transfers it directly into resident GPU pages. Otherwise, if the fixed","-host-backed GPU footprint and host source blocks fit, the request imports into","-the host tier. There is no context-length threshold or other heuristic, and a","-request waiting for capacity retains its choice across admission retries.","-","-A host import reads through a bounded decoder-GPU staging pool before copying","-into registered host memory. Pages needed immediately are mirrored into their","-resident destinations during that copy. Both landing targets then use the same","-fused decode resolver described above.","+For supported P/D configurations, NIXL imports offloaded main KV into the host","+tier. After an import completes, the coordinator schedules host-to-device","+copies for the tail page and promotes additional imported pages using free","+GPU blocks above the transition watermark. Promoted pages retain their host","+backing and follow the normal residency policy. Indexer KV is transferred to","+its GPU cache group."," "," ## Indexer KV offloading"," "," HiSparse does not keep a private CPU copy of indexer KV. The indexer remains a"," normal prefix-cacheable GPU cache group. If `OffloadingConnector` is configured"," with HiSparse, it stores and restores that group through the generic KV","-offloading path; HiSparse continues to own only the sparse MLA host tier.","+offloading path; HiSparse continues to own only the main sparse-attention host tier."," "," The two prefix sources can have different hit lengths. When the HiSparse host"," prefix extends beyond the GPU-resident indexer prefix, the scheduler asks"," `OffloadingConnector` to restore only the missing indexer suffix, capped at the"," host prefix boundary. If that suffix is unavailable, all groups fall back to","-the shorter prefix they share. NIXL P/D transfers continue to place indexer KV","-directly in its GPU group.","+the shorter prefix they share."," "," ## Spill transaction"," "],"additions":40,"deletions":20,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_qsa_reference.py","lines":["@@ -23,8 +23,11 @@"," from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia.ops import qsa_indexer as qsa_indexer_ops"," from vllm.platforms import current_platform"," from vllm.triton_utils import HAS_TRITON","+from vllm.v1.kv_cache_interface import AttentionSpec"," from vllm.v1.worker.utils import clear_layer_kv_caches"," ","+from ...utils import create_new_process_for_each_test","+"," requires_qsa_kernels = pytest.mark.skipif(","     not current_platform.is_cuda() or not HAS_TRITON,","     reason=\"QSA kernels require CUDA and Triton\",","@@ -35,6 +38,77 @@"," )"," "," ","+_HISPARSE_KV_TRANSFER_CONFIG = {","+    \"kv_connector\": \"HiSparseConnector\",","+    \"kv_role\": \"kv_both\",","+    \"kv_connector_extra_config\": {\"host_pool_gib\": 1 / 64},","+}","+_TINY_QSA_TEXT_CONFIG = {","+    \"hidden_size\": 256,","+    \"num_attention_heads\": 24,","+    \"num_key_value_heads\": 2,","+    \"head_dim\": 64,","+    \"num_experts\": 4,","+    \"num_experts_per_tok\": 2,","+    \"indexer_n_heads\": 8,","+    \"indexer_kv_heads\": 1,","+    \"indexer_head_dim\": 128,","+    \"indexer_compress_ratio\": 4,","+    \"indexer_budget\": 2048,","+}","+","+","+@requires_qsa_kernels","+def test_qsa_hisparse_starts_with_automatic_cache_layout(","+    tmp_path, vllm_runner, monkeypatch","+):","+    from transformers import Qwen4ExpConfig","+","+    from vllm import SamplingParams","+","+    monkeypatch.delenv(\"VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT\", raising=False)","+    Qwen4ExpConfig(","+        architectures=[\"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\"],","+        text_config={","+            **_TINY_QSA_TEXT_CONFIG,","+            \"vocab_size\": 128,","+            \"num_hidden_layers\": 2,","+            \"layer_types\": [\"linear_attention\", \"indexed_attention\"],","+            \"linear_num_key_heads\": 2,","+            \"linear_num_value_heads\": 4,","+            \"output_gate_type\": \"sigmoid\",","+            \"moe_intermediate_size\": 64,","+            \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\": 64,","+            \"hc_lowrank\": 28,","+            \"mtp_num_hidden_layers\": 0,","+        },","+    ).save_pretrained(tmp_path)","+    with vllm_runner(","+        str(tmp_path),","+        language_model_only=True,","+        skip_tokenizer_init=True,","+        load_format=\"dummy\",","+        dtype=\"bfloat16\",","+        kv_cache_dtype=\"fp8_e4m3\",","+        attention_config={\"hisparse_config\": {}, \"indexer_kv_dtype\": \"bf16\"},","+        kv_transfer_config=_HISPARSE_KV_TRANSFER_CONFIG,","+        enable_chunked_prefill=True,","+        enable_prefix_caching=False,","+        async_scheduling=False,","+        enforce_eager=True,","+        max_model_len=128,","+        max_num_seqs=2,","+        kv_cache_memory_bytes=128 * 1024**2,","+    ) as runner:","+        (result,) = runner.llm.generate(","+            {\"prompt_token_ids\": [1, 2, 3, 4]},","+            SamplingParams(","+                temperature=0, max_tokens=2, ignore_eos=True, detokenize=False","+            ),","+        )","+        assert len(result.outputs[0].token_ids) == 2","+","+"," def test_qsa_mtp_index_share_updates_cache_but_skips_selection(","     monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,"," ) -> None:","@@ -105,6 +179,7 @@ def test_qsa_mtp_index_share_updates_cache_but_skips_selection(","         attn=attn,","         qkv=torch.zeros(2, 4),","         slot_mapping=torch.arange(2),","+        main_kv_cache=attn.kv_cache,","     )"," ","     assert actual is rows","@@ -723,6 +798,54 @@ def make_buffers() -> tuple[torch.Tensor, torch.Tensor, torch.Tensor, torch.Tens","     torch.testing.assert_close(actual_k_work, expected_k_work)"," "," ","+@requires_qsa_kernels","+@create_new_process_for_each_test(\"spawn\")","+def test_qsa_sparse_attention_warmup_covers_different_cache_pools() -> None:","+    \"\"\"Host and resident pool sizes must reuse the warmed logical-index kernel.\"\"\"","+    from vllm.triton_utils import triton","+","+    torch.manual_seed(7)","+    # The packed selection's final column contains the valid count.","+    q = torch.randn(3, 24, 64, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.bfloat16)","+    gate = torch.randn_like(q)","+    cache = torch.randn(17, 16, 2, 128, device=\"cuda\", dtype=q.dtype)","+    block_table = torch.zeros(2, 1, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int32)","+    requests = torch.tensor([0, 1, 1], device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int32)","+    indices = torch.full((3, 32), -1, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int32)","+    indices[:, :16] = torch.arange(16, device=\"cuda\")","+    indices[:, -1] = 16","+    k_cache, v_cache = cache.split(64, dim=-1)","+    expected = _qsa_sparse_paged_attention_reference(","+        q, k_cache, v_cache, indices[:, :-1], block_table, requests, 64**-0.5","+    ) * torch.sigmoid(gate)","+","+    qsa_ops.warmup_qsa_sparse_paged_attention(","+        cache.transpose(1, 2),","+        block_table,","+        num_query_heads=24,","+        selection_width=31,","+    )","+","+    def fail_compile(**kwargs):","+        pytest.fail(f\"QSA compiled after warmup: {kwargs.get('fn')}\")","+","+    # Restore Triton's compilation observer after checking the runtime calls.","+    with pytest.MonkeyPatch.context() as patch:","+        patch.setattr(triton.knobs.runtime, \"jit_post_compile_hook\", fail_compile)","+        for num_blocks in (16, 1, 17):","+            actual = qsa_ops.qsa_sparse_paged_attention(","+                q,","+                k_cache[:num_blocks],","+                v_cache[:num_blocks],","+                indices,","+                block_table,","+                requests,","+                use_prefill_config=True,","+                output_gate=gate,","+            )","+            torch.testing.assert_close(actual, expected, rtol=2e-2, atol=2e-2)","+","+"," @requires_qsa_kernels"," @pytest.mark.parametrize(","     (\"decode_query_len\", \"num_requests\"),","@@ -1266,6 +1389,307 @@ def test_qsa_fp8_kernel_correctness(","     assert not actual[-1].any()"," "," ","+@requires_qsa_kernels","+# 33 FP8 rows x 2 KV heads cross the Blackwell FP8 decode-kernel threshold.","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"fp8\", [False, True], ids=[\"bf16\", \"large-fp8\"])","+def test_qsa_attention_consumes_hisparse_physical_indices(fp8: bool) -> None:","+    \"\"\"Resolved HiSparse rows bypass the logical block table on padded pages.\"\"\"","+    from vllm.v1.hisparse.runtime import PagedCacheView","+","+    if fp8 and not current_platform.has_device_capability(89):","+        pytest.skip(\"Native FP8 pointers require sm_89 or newer\")","+","+    torch.manual_seed(7)","+    num_blocks, block_size, num_kv_heads, head_dim = 4, 16, 2, 64","+    row_width = num_kv_heads * 2 * head_dim","+    block_stride = (2 * block_size + 1) * row_width","+    storage_dtype = torch.uint8 if fp8 else torch.bfloat16","+    k_scale, v_scale = (0.5, 2.0) if fp8 else (1.0, 1.0)","+    backing = torch.full(","+        (num_blocks * block_stride,), 7, device=\"cuda\", dtype=storage_dtype","+    )","+    view = PagedCacheView.bind(","+        backing.view(torch.uint8),","+        dtype=backing.dtype,","+        row_width=row_width,","+        byte_offset=block_size * row_width * backing.element_size(),","+        block_stride=block_stride * backing.element_size(),","+        num_blocks=num_blocks,","+        block_size=block_size,","+    )","+    original = torch.randn(","+        num_blocks,","+        block_size,","+        num_kv_heads,","+        2 * head_dim,","+        device=\"cuda\",","+        dtype=torch.bfloat16,","+    )","+    original_key, original_value = original.split(head_dim, dim=-1)","+    if fp8:","+        original_key = (original_key.float() / k_scale).to(torch.float8_e4m3fn)","+        original_value = (original_value.float() / v_scale).to(torch.float8_e4m3fn)","+    stored = torch.cat(","+        (original_key.view(storage_dtype), original_value.view(storage_dtype)), dim=-1","+    )","+    view.cache.copy_(stored.flatten(2))","+    attention_cache = view.attention_cache.unflatten(-1, (num_kv_heads, 2 * head_dim))","+    key_cache, value_cache = attention_cache.split(head_dim, dim=-1)","+    if fp8:","+        key_cache = key_cache.view(torch.float8_e4m3fn)","+        value_cache = value_cache.view(torch.float8_e4m3fn)","+    selected = torch.tensor(","+        [[55, 2, 43, -1, -1], [16, 63, 33, 6, 30], [-1, -1, -1, -1, -1]],","+        device=\"cuda\",","+        dtype=torch.int32,","+    ).repeat(11 if fp8 else 1, 1)","+    counts = (selected >= 0).sum(dim=1, keepdim=True, dtype=torch.int32)","+    physical_rows = torch.where(","+        selected >= 0,","+        selected // block_size * view.attention_block_stride + selected % block_size,","+        -1,","+    )","+    # Counts stay in the logical packed buffer; resolved rows have no count.","+    logical_packed = torch.cat((selected, counts), dim=1)","+    num_rows = selected.shape[0]","+    q = torch.randn(num_rows, 24, head_dim, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.bfloat16)","+    output_gate = torch.randn_like(q)","+    token_to_req = torch.zeros(num_rows, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int32)","+    identity = torch.arange(num_blocks, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int32)[None]","+    expected = _qsa_sparse_paged_attention_reference(","+        q,","+        original_key,","+        original_value,","+        selected,","+        identity,","+        token_to_req,","+        head_dim**-0.5,","+        k_scale=k_scale,","+        v_scale=v_scale,","+    ) * torch.sigmoid(output_gate)","+","+    actual = qsa_ops.qsa_sparse_paged_attention(","+        q,","+        key_cache,","+        value_cache,","+        physical_rows,","+        identity.roll(1, dims=1),","+        token_to_req,","+        use_prefill_config=False,","+        k_scale=k_scale,","+        v_scale=v_scale,","+        output_gate=output_gate,","+        valid_counts=logical_packed[:, -1],","+    )","+","+    torch.testing.assert_close(actual, expected, rtol=2e-2, atol=2e-2)","+","+","+@requires_qsa_kernels","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"all_context_pages_resident\", [False, True])","+def test_qsa_hisparse_prefill_ignores_unused_request_table_rows(","+    tmp_path, dist_init, workspace_init, all_context_pages_resident: bool","+) -> None:","+    \"\"\"Unequal active lengths and reordered state slots keep the right KV rows.\"\"\"","+    from dataclasses import replace","+","+    from transformers import Qwen4ExpTextConfig","+","+    from vllm.config import AttentionConfig, HiSparseConfig, set_current_vllm_config","+    from vllm.engine.arg_utils import EngineArgs","+    from vllm.forward_context import set_forward_context","+    from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia.qsa import Qwen4ExpQSAAttention","+    from vllm.utils.torch_utils import set_default_torch_dtype","+    from vllm.v1.attention.backend import CommonAttentionMetadata","+    from vllm.v1.hisparse.runtime import (","+        allocate_pinned_host_pool,","+        release_pinned_state,","+    )","+","+    torch.manual_seed(7)","+    num_blocks, block_size, heads, dim = 8, 16, 2, 64","+    config = Qwen4ExpTextConfig(","+        **_TINY_QSA_TEXT_CONFIG,","+        architectures=[\"Qwen4ExpForCausalLM\"],","+        num_hidden_layers=1,","+        layer_types=[\"full_attention\"],","+        intermediate_size=512,","+        partial_rotary_factor=1.0,","+        ple_layer_ids=[],","+    )","+    config.save_pretrained(tmp_path)","+    vllm_config = EngineArgs(","+        model=str(tmp_path),","+        load_format=\"dummy\",","+        skip_tokenizer_init=True,","+        dtype=\"bfloat16\",","+        kv_cache_dtype=\"bfloat16\",","+        block_size=block_size,","+        max_model_len=128,","+        max_num_batched_tokens=128,","+        max_num_seqs=4,","+        enforce_eager=True,","+        async_scheduling=False,","+        enable_prefix_caching=False,","+        enable_chunked_prefill=False,","+        attention_config=AttentionConfig(","+            hisparse_config=HiSparseConfig(),","+            indexer_kv_dtype=\"bf16\",","+        ),","+        kv_transfer_config=_HISPARSE_KV_TRANSFER_CONFIG,","+    ).create_engine_config()","+    with (","+        set_current_vllm_config(vllm_config),","+        set_default_torch_dtype(torch.bfloat16),","+        torch.device(\"cuda\"),","+    ):","+        owner = Qwen4ExpQSAAttention(","+            vllm_config=vllm_config,","+            config=config,","+            layer_id=0,","+            topk_indices_buffer=torch.empty(","+                vllm_config.scheduler_config.max_num_batched_tokens,","+                _qwen4_exp_model.get_qsa_topk_buffer_width(config),","+                dtype=torch.int32,","+            ),","+            prefix=\"model.layers.0.self_attn\",","+        )","+        owner.process_weights_after_loading()","+    row_width = heads * 2 * dim","+    original = torch.randn(","+        num_blocks, block_size, heads, 2 * dim, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.bfloat16","+    )","+    original[6].fill_(17)","+    original[7].fill_(-19)","+    backing = original.flatten().clone()","+    source_table = torch.tensor(","+        [[1, 2, 0], [3, 4, 5], [6, 6, 6], [7, 7, 7]],","+        device=\"cuda\",","+        dtype=torch.int32,","+    )","+    resident_table = source_table.clone()","+    if not all_context_pages_resident:","+        resident_table[1, 0] = 0","+    # Residency uses persistent state rows, independent of this batch's order.","+    state_indices = torch.tensor([1, 0, 2, 3], device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int32)","+    resident_table = resident_table.index_select(0, state_indices)","+    slots = torch.tensor([31, 32, 79, 80], device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int64)","+    requests = torch.tensor([0, 0, 1, 1], device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int32)","+    positions = torch.tensor([15, 16, 31, 32], device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int64)","+    selection = torch.arange(33, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int32).expand(4, -1)","+    selection = selection.masked_fill(selection > positions[:, None], -1)","+    q = torch.zeros(4, 24, dim, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.bfloat16)","+    key = torch.zeros(4, heads, dim, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.bfloat16)","+    value = torch.randn_like(key)","+    hidden = torch.eye(4, 256, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.bfloat16)","+    # Real projections produce Q=K=gate=0 and the specified V rows. Output","+    # projection selects two Q heads from each KV head, exercising both shards.","+    output_columns = torch.cat((torch.arange(128), torch.arange(768, 896))).cuda()","+    with torch.no_grad():","+        for parameter in owner.parameters():","+            parameter.zero_()","+        owner.qkv_proj.weight[","+            2 * owner.q_size + owner.kv_size : 2 * owner.q_size + 2 * owner.kv_size,","+            :4,","+        ].copy_(value.flatten(1).transpose(0, 1))","+        owner.o_proj.weight[torch.arange(256, device=\"cuda\"), output_columns] = 1","+    common = CommonAttentionMetadata(","+        num_actual_tokens=4,","+        num_reqs=2,","+        max_query_len=2,","+        query_start_loc=torch.tensor([0, 2, 4], device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int32),","+        query_start_loc_cpu=torch.tensor([0, 2, 4], dtype=torch.int32),","+        max_seq_len=33,","+        seq_lens=torch.tensor([17, 33], device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int32),","+        seq_lens_cpu_upper_bound=torch.tensor([17, 33], dtype=torch.int32),","+        block_table_tensor=source_table[:2],","+        slot_mapping=slots,","+    )","+    builder = owner.get_attn_backend().get_builder_cls()(","+        owner.get_kv_cache_config(vllm_config).spec,","+        [owner.layer_name],","+        vllm_config,","+        torch.device(\"cuda\"),","+    )","+    all_metadata = {owner.layer_name: builder.build(0, common)}","+    for side_cache, table in (","+        (owner.indexer.raw_key_cache, torch.tensor([[1], [2]], dtype=torch.int32)),","+        (owner.indexer.compressed_key_cache, source_table[:2]),","+    ):","+        spec = side_cache.get_kv_cache_config(vllm_config).spec","+        assert isinstance(spec, AttentionSpec)","+        side_cache.bind_kv_cache(","+            torch.zeros(","+                num_blocks, 1, spec.num_states, 128, device=\"cuda\", dtype=spec.dtype","+            )","+        )","+        all_metadata[side_cache.prefix] = QSAIndexerMetadataBuilder(","+            spec, [side_cache.prefix], vllm_config, torch.device(\"cuda\")","+        ).build(0, replace(common, block_table_tensor=table.cuda()))","+    cache = owner.hisparse_cache","+    assert cache is not None","+    runtime = cache.runtime","+    cache.bind_cache(","+        backing.view(torch.uint8),","+        byte_offset=0,","+        block_stride=block_size * row_width * backing.element_size(),","+        num_blocks=num_blocks,","+        block_size=block_size,","+        block_table=resident_table,","+        slot_mapping=slots,","+    )","+    assert cache.view is not None","+    cache.source_block_table = source_table","+    runtime.request_state_indices = state_indices","+    cache.all_context_pages_resident = all_context_pages_resident","+    owner.bind_kv_cache(original.transpose(1, 2))","+    host, registered = allocate_pinned_host_pool(original.nbytes)","+    try:","+        host_rows = host.view(original.dtype).view(-1, row_width)","+        host_rows.copy_(original.flatten(2).reshape(-1, row_width).cpu())","+        runtime.bind_source_cache(host_rows, registered_host_pool=registered)","+        if not all_context_pages_resident:","+            # Only host retains this selected history page.","+            cache.view.cache[3].fill_(29)","+        new_rows = torch.cat((key, value), dim=-1)","+        reference = original.clone()","+        ref